WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.286
There is a long-standing intuition that each
attention head can specialize,

00:00:03.366 --> 00:00:06.651
learning a different kind of relationship,

00:00:06.731 --> 00:00:10.017
much as convolutional kernels learn different features.

00:00:10.097 --> 00:00:13.382
If that is true,

00:00:13.462 --> 00:00:16.748
then a Transformer mixing several attention types
could learn a richer set of relationships

00:00:16.828 --> 00:00:20.113
and outperform any single-attention model.

00:00:20.193 --> 00:00:23.479
This paper takes that intuition seriously and asks
directly whether the optimal attention

00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:26.844
for a task is actually a mixture of different attentions,

00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:30.210
rather than assuming the answer.
